From b41b71f42f31422fd77fe38c35f40706eae1fab8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tong_1001 <sxt1001@qq.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 10:18:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix: match conflict processes by exact /proc cmdline argv
 instead of ps aux substring

check_conflict() scanned `ps aux` output with a raw substring match on task_start.
When task_start was a generic word (e.g. python3, sh), conflict=kill killed every
process whose command line merely contained the word, including unrelated root
services; editors such as `vim /usr/bin/xxx` were also misjudged as conflict instances.

Rework the detection:
- read /proc/<pid>/cmdline and require the process argv to equal shlex.split(task_start)
exactly: same command and same arguments, no more and no less. A process is not a conflict
when its command line merely contains task_start as a substring, or runs with different
or extra arguments;
- non-absolute-path commands are fine: the cmdline is compared verbatim, so a generic
word (e.g. python3) only matches an identical argv, never a broader set of processes;
- recheck the cmdline right before kill to avoid killing a recycled pid;
- never treat the syssentry process itself as a conflict;
- return False with error logs on /proc or shlex failures instead of raising.

Both InspectTask and PeriodTask share this method, so oneshot and period tasks are fixed
at once. Document the exact-argv matching rule in the conflict row of the developer guides
and add unit tests (selftest/test/test_check_conflict.py) covering exact matching with and
without arguments, substring and extra-args non-matches, recycled pid, self pid and error
paths.

Co-Authored-By: GLM-5.2
